This Kotlin Multiplatform library combines specification implementations with
ports of permissively licensed compression code.

The DEFLATE inflate path is an altered Kotlin translation of Mark Adler's puff
(2002-2013), via KiteTorrent and libtorrent. puff carries a zlib-style license,
not a public-domain dedication; its original notice is retained in Inflate.kt.
The DEFLATE encoder originated in KitePDF's FlateDecode encoder and its
length-limited Huffman construction follows zlib's trees.c (Jean-loup Gailly and
Mark Adler). Deflate.kt retains the zlib copyright and license notice.

Format references consulted for porting (study only, not redistributed; see
reference/REFERENCES.md) are each under permissive licenses: zlib (zlib), XZ for Java
(0BSD / public domain), Apache Commons Compress (Apache-2.0), lz4 (BSD-2), zstd
(BSD-3), brotli (MIT), snappy (BSD-3).

RAR / ACE / StuffIt are deliberately excluded: the UnRAR license forbids using its
source to build a RAR-compatible compressor, and no clean open reference exists for
ACE/StuffIt. ArchiveKodec will never create RAR archives.
